  "basis": "The dashboard legend is a vertical color ramp labeled 'High' at the top (value 100, pale yellow) and 'Low' at the bottom (value 0, dark red). This establishes that paler fills indicate higher prevalence and darker fills indicate lower prevalence. Comparing the three candidate states: New Jersey (NJ) is filled with a very pale yellow, placing it at the high end of the scale (near 100). Pennsylvania (PA) is filled with a very dark red, placing it at the low end of the scale (near 0). Delaware (DE) is filled with a pale yellow, also at the high end. Since the routing criterion is the 'highest-prevalence state' and the workflow is 'priority follow-up', the record must be for a high-prevalence state. NJ is high-prevalence (pale yellow) and its corresponding option is 'priority follow-up'. PA is low-prevalence (dark red). DE is high-prevalence but its option is 'routine monitoring'. Therefore, the NJ record is the correct one to open for the priority follow-up workflow.",
  "option_label": "Open New Jersey (NJ) prevalence detail for priority follow-up"
}
